    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionSection">Media conversion</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionDefaultsCrf">Default CRF (quality)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionCrf">CRF (0 = use default)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionCrfToolTip">H.264 constant rate factor (0–51). Lower values yield higher quality and larger files. Set 0 to use the default CRF above.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionCrfDescription">The CRF sets the trade-off between MP4 quality and file size: a lower value improves image quality (larger file), a higher value reduces file size (lower quality). 23 is a good starting point for most users.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionAlphaNote">Output uses H.264 yuv420p, which does not preserve transparency. This is acceptable for most animated backgrounds and covers, which rarely rely on alpha.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionAnimatedWebp">Animated WebP</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionWebm">WebM</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionApng">Animated PNG (APNG)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionGif">Animated GIF</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionUseAutoFramerate">Use source frame timing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionFixedFramerate">Fixed frame rate (fps)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionForceReencode">Always re-encode to H.264</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionForceReencodeToolTip">When disabled, FFmpeg attempts to copy the video stream when the WebM is already H.264 compatible.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionCrfInvalid">Media conversion CRF must be 0 (inherit default) or between 0 and 51. Default CRF must be between 0 and 51.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCBcMediaConversionFramerateInvalid">Media conversion frame rate must be between 1 and 120 fps.</sys:String>

